.TH GPS-STATION-DESKTOP 1 "October 2026" "gps-station" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gps-station-desktop \- keep running ham programs on the GPS grid square
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gps-station-desktop
.RB [ \-\-radio
.IR host:port ]
.RB [ \-\-gpsd
.IR host:port ]
.RB [ \-\-chars " 4|6]"
.RB [ \-\-show ]
.br
.B gps-station-desktop \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
A tray icon for the desktop of an sBitx or zBitx, started at login from
.IR /etc/xdg/autostart .
The icon's crosshair shows the GPS fix (grey none, blue 2D, green 3D), a
dot shows where the time comes from (green the GPS, blue the Internet, red
not synchronized), and an amber "!" appears when a ticked program's grid
differs from the GPS.
.PP
Clicking the icon opens a window with the GPS grid, the receiver's state,
what the clock follows, a map of the satellites, and a row for each
supported program that is running: the radio, WSJT-X, JTDX, JS8Call,
fldigi, QSSTV and GridTracker.
Each row is marked as matching the GPS, stale, set by hand, or unreadable.
Only ticked programs are changed: a stale grid is updated, a grid set by
hand is kept until the GPS moves to another square or
.B Update
is pressed.
When a ticked program can't be updated, a desktop notification says which
of its settings to change, once per launch.
Programs that aren't running are never touched.
.PP
WSJT-X is updated with a UDP Location message (it needs Accept UDP
requests and AutoGrid) and JS8Call through its TCP API (TCP server API
and Accept TCP requests). JTDX, fldigi and QSSTV can't be changed while
running. To share WSJT-X's UDP stream with GridTracker, send it to a
multicast address such as 239.255.0.1 on the lo interface.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-radio " host:port"
The radio software's TCP port (default 127.0.0.1:8081).
.TP
.BI \-\-gpsd " host:port"
gpsd (default 127.0.0.1:2947).
.TP
.BR \-\-chars " 4|6"
Grid length (default 6).
.TP
.B \-\-show
Open the window at start.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/gps-station/apps.json
Which programs are ticked.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gps-station (8)
.PP
https://github.com/jchonig/bitx-gps-station
